An unknown period is a usage error at parse time, with no request.
-- args --
body
export-blood-pressure
--period
weekly

-- table stdout --
-- table stderr --
Usage: gccli body export-blood-pressure [flags]

Save the blood pressure report as a PDF.

Garmin creates the report and the command waits for it, up to two minutes.
The report is a PDF: Garmin also accepts JSON as a format but returns a PDF for
it. The period fixes the range, because Garmin answers DATA_NOT_FOUND for any
other length. An existing output file is overwritten. For the readings as data,
use body blood-pressure.

Flags:
  -h, --help              Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json              Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain             Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header            Print the column names as the first line of --plain
                          output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"      Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING    Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"      Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                          elevations and weights in table and plain output:
                          auto (Garmin profile), metric, statute_us, statute_uk
                          ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version           Print version information.

      --period="daily"    Report layout and range: daily (1 day), seven-days,
                          four-weeks (28 days) or yearly (52 weeks).
      --end="today"       Last day of the report (YYYY-MM-DD, today, yesterday,
                          3d). Defaults to today.
  -o, --output=STRING     Output file path (default:
                          blood_pressure_{period}_{end}.pdf).

